Route: web `/` resolves to `AppRoute.dashboard` via `AppRouteParser.aliases["/"]` (pre-existing).
The page is registered through `DashboardRouteRegistration.registry` and threaded into
`TeslaSyncApp.routeHostRegistry` (onNavigate→selection, onPrint→.teslaSyncPrintRequested,
onOpenThemePicker→.settings). Until now `.dashboard` rendered the "page pending" state.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARCHITECTURE (mirrors the sibling GlancePage)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  · @Observable DashboardPageModel (main-actor) — no networking in the view (ADR-004).
  · DashboardDataSource seam (loadAuthStatus / loadVehicles / syncVehicles); production binds
    the KMP core, Sample default + DEBUG doubles (SyncNeeded / NotConnected / Failing) drive
    every data state.
  · Pure derivations in DashboardModels.swift (onboarding copy branch, customize-hint gate,
    undo/redo enablement, seeded widget layout) kept SwiftUI-free + unit-tested.
  · Design tokens only (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSTone), shared P3
    components (TSGlassPanel, TSCard, TSAlertBanner, TSLiveStaleDataBanner, TSEmptyState,
    TSErrorDisplay, TSButton, TSIconBox). No raw colors/typography, no web cloning.
  · Adaptive: width-capped centered column (macOS/iPad regular) ↔ full compact width; banners
    and the widget grid reflow via LazyVGrid(adaptive:).

