CODE REVIEW (self-review agent) — 2 issues found + fixed before commit
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. (Medium) Edit-mode "Add Widget" was a no-op (called setEditMode(true) while already in edit
   mode); model.addWidget(_:) had no UI call site, so a removed widget could only return via
   Undo/Reset. FIX: added DashboardAddWidgetSheet (web `WidgetPicker`) listing the addable
   widgets; the toolbar "Add Widget" + the customize-hint CTA now present it and call
   model.addWidget(_:). A blank dashboard renders DashboardEmptyLayout with an Add action.
2. (Low) Templates "New Dashboard" called resetToDefault() — identical to Reset (restored the
   seeded widgets), silently discarding customization. FIX: added model.newBlankDashboard()
   (web `__blank__`/createDashboard) which starts an empty layout (undoable), distinct from
   Reset; the empty grid degrades to DashboardEmptyLayout (never a dead region).
   Both fixes are unit-tested (testNewBlankDashboardClearsLayout, testAddWidgetAppendsAfterRemove,
   testAddableWidgetsExcludesPresent) and re-verified green (build + 23/23 + lint).

